_severities":["critical","high"],"command":"env AP_REVIEWER_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5 AP_REVIEWER_EFFORT=low uv run python -B docs/examples/reviewers/claude_review.py","executor":"command","max_findings":50,"require_command_for":[]},"stage":{"max_attempts":5,"max_restarts":5,"timeout_seconds":660},"worktree":{"copy_files":[".env"],"mode":"in_place","root":null,"setup_command":null}},"findings":[{"action":"ask_user","code_owned":false,"detail":"merge_telemetry skips the repository's `path` before validation, whatever its value. So `path = 5` or `path = []` in `.agentic-preflight.toml` only prints the 'ignoring' warning and never raises the ConfigError that TelemetrySection would raise. The intent says invalid values in the repository section must stay errors. A bad repository `path` is now the one exception, and that is a judgement call the intent leaves open.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F001","line":364,"path":"agentic_preflight/config.py","response_note":"User decision: a repository [telemetry] path is ignored with a warning whatever its value. The key has no effect, so a bad value in it should not stop the user's commands from loading; the warning names the file.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"dismissed","suggestion":"Decide whether a repository `path` should still be type-checked. If so, validate it as `str | None` before dropping it, or keep the warning and say in the docs that the repository `path` is not validated.","title":"An invalid repository [telemetry] path is dropped instead of reported","unit":"U0006"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"When the user file's `telemetry` is not a table (for example `telemetry = 5`), `merged` becomes `{}` and the repository's section replaces it. Validation then passes, and the user's malformed value is never reported. Without a repository section, the same user file fails to load. hooklog.fallback_section calls merge_telemetry and has the same gap.","fix_commit":"4b6b2dc9fc430f3b553834e9cd493492cd08b8e7","id":"F002","line":362,"path":"agentic_preflight/config.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Return the user value unchanged when it is not a dict, so validation still reports it against the user file. Or raise when `user` is neither None nor a dict.","title":"A malformed user [telemetry] value is silently discarded when the repository has a section","unit":"U0006"},{"action":"ask_user","code_owned":false,"detail":"merge_telemetry drops the repository's `path` key without checking its value. A repository `path = 5` or `path = []` therefore produces only the 'ignoring [telemetry] path' warning, and validation never sees it. The intent says invalid values in the repository section remain errors, and COMPATIBILITY.md and docs/configuration.md say so too. For `path`, that is no longer true. The tests cover only invalid `hook_log` values and unknown keys.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F003","line":368,"path":"agentic_preflight/config.py","response_note":"User decision (asked this session): a repository [telemetry] path is ignored with a warning whatever its value. The docs and docstring wording that implied every invalid repository value errors is corrected in the next commit to name mirror, hook_log, and unknown keys.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"dismissed","suggestion":"Decide whether an invalid repository `path` should still fail. If it should, validate the value first (for example with TelemetrySection.model_validate({'path': value})) and drop it only when it is valid. If it should not, add `path` as an exception in the docs.","title":"An invalid repository [telemetry] path is now dropped with a warning instead of being reported as an error","unit":"U0006"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"Source attribution uses `value is user_values[name]`. Python reuses the same objects for small ints and for bools. If the user file and the repository both set `hook_log = 3`, the merged value is the repository's 3, but it is the same object as the user's 3. The error then names only the user file, even though the repository set the value that applied.","fix_commit":"76089404b121e606091598db5877e00dc5baf007","id":"F004","line":428,"path":"agentic_preflight/config.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Track which keys merge_telemetry took from the repository, for example by returning or computing `set(repo) - {'path'} - {k for k in ('mirror','hook_log') if repo.get(k) is True}`. Attribute a key to the user file only when the repository did not supply it.","title":"An identity check can blame the user file for a bad value the repository also set","unit":"U0007"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"merge_telemetry imports sys inside the warning branch. That differs from the module-level imports used elsewhere in the module, and there is no circular-import reason for it.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F005","line":370,"path":"agentic_preflight/config.py","response_note":"Fixed by 7608940 (registered for F004): config.py now imports sys once at module level and every local import is gone.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"dismissed","suggestion":"Move `import sys` to the module's imports.","title":"`import sys` is inside the function instead of at module level","unit":"U0006"}],"fingerprint":{"base_tree_sha":"8781de91bef2081f62309dc01bb8f4a0b81a13ad","config_sha256":"64ebd95cb7eea63aa3314d30f8066a3b3fc1290f8222e60e9235d3cc1cbaecc9","configuration_supported":true,"diff_sha256":"c49230c2ed2b8ab69db05d18bcf5ed106a8cdecc25a3d6a8a634b9edb831d078","excluded_files":[],"executor":"command","grounding_sha256":"575175cdb1479912620ebba8e9deefc1cb5ba31679eeaef417594ad3ee7ea86d","head_tree_sha":"2ebb24f68f844e2d5c13183daf933ce80aefc4f5","intent_sha256":"20404faf25409620f130308e0aa855c1e514cbd00d0476e1deab762f2122fe4a","version":2},"finished_at":"2026-11-02T05:16:34Z","head_sha":"76089404b121e606091598db58